##In Omarchy docker comes with pre installed

##I run Command

-docker --version

its show the version of installed docker.

Then i run:

-docker info

### i get server : Permission denied while trying to connect to the docker API 
at unix:///var/run/docker.sock

So want to check the permission of /var/run/docker.sock

-ls -l /var/run/docker.sock

-then stat -c '%A %U %G %n' /var/run/docker.sock

Output:

srw-rw---- root docker /var/run/docker.sock

Here totally two groups have permission one is root another one docker 

Need to check  current user naoh have in these groups or not

-groups noah

i found current user noah not in docker groups as well as root.

so i add naoh into docker

-sudo usermod -aG docker noah

Before that i run this command for check how many users in docker group 

-getent group docker 

 output:

docker:x:966:

so its shows no users under docker group

once i add noah into docker groups output will be

output:

-docker:x:966:noah (966 its a GID)


For checking i was run

-docker run hello-world

I got welcome text on CLI

then i run 

-docker images (For findout what are the images i have in docker)

then

-docker ps (for find container but its only show when  they on run)

so i run

-docker ps -a (a means all container)

## Pull a image on docker UBUNTU 24.04

- docker pull ubuntu:24.04

for run a image container

- docker run -dit --name linux-admin ubuntu:24.04

here :

docker - command line client

run - create and start a new container

-d - detatched mode means runs on background

-i - keep STDIN open (idk what is it)

-t - allocate a terminal

--name - of the conatiner and image


=============================================================================

After successfully run the container 

- docker exce -it linux-admin bash 

exec - means send a commnad to server

-i - keep input

-t - give us terminal 

-linux-admin - container name

bash - start the bash shell
